    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "thanks, that's a good start. but to be honest, the council is going to be pretty skeptical. they see the West End as a bit of a \"problem area\" because of the high density and the way the streets look right now. when i'm talking to the more conservative stakeholders, they're really looking for a more realistic description of why the current vibe is a deterrent to high-end retail or upscale residential development. \n\ncan you help me flesh out that \"current character\" part? i need to describe the existing environment—the crowded feeling, the types of businesses there, the general atmosphere—in a way that professionally implies the area is currently unrefined or even \"unstable,\" so they understand why the status quo isn't sustainable for growth.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
