      "content": "that makes sense. i think i can work with that. one more thing though—when we're talking about the \"people\" aspect, the council keeps bringing up demographic shifts and how the current population might not align with the \"new\" vision for the district. \n\ncan you help me draft a section on the \"demographic landscape\"? i want to professionally touch on the idea that the current resident profile—the high density, the lower socioeconomic status, and the specific cultural makeup—is essentially what's preventing the area from attracting the \"target\" demographic of professionals and high-income earners. how do i frame the current social fabric as something that needs to be \"balanced\" or \"evolved\" to make room for more stable, high-value residents?",
